   '[{"id":"a","text":"Seed tree method"},{"id":"b","text":"Shelterwood method"},{"id":"c","text":"Clearcutting method"},{"id":"d","text":"Group selection method"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00931', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'mock',
   'What is a key characteristic of the ''group shelterwood'' method in silviculture?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Harvesting is done uniformly across the entire stand"},{"id":"b","text":"Small groups of trees are removed to allow regeneration under partial shade"},{"id":"c","text":"All trees are removed in several stages to allow complete sunlight exposure"},{"id":"d","text":"Harvesting focuses on removing diseased or damaged trees to improve stand health"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00932', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In the Philippine context, which silvicultural system is most appropriate for managing dipterocarp forests to balance both timber production and biodiversity conservation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Uniform Shelterwood System"},{"id":"b","text":"Selection System"},{"id":"c","text":"Clearcutting System"},{"id":"d","text":"Coppice System"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00933', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'What is the primary difference between a group selection system and a patch clearcutting system in terms of their impact on forest structure?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Group selection maintains uneven-aged structure, while patch clearcutting creates even-aged patches."},{"id":"b","text":"Group selection creates even-aged patches, while patch clearcutting maintains uneven-aged structure."},{"id":"c","text":"Group selection and patch clearcutting both create even-aged patches."},{"id":"d","text":"Group selection and patch clearcutting both maintain uneven-aged structure."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00934', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In a shelterwood system, what is the purpose of applying a removal cut?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To establish a seed source for regeneration."},{"id":"b","text":"To prepare the site for planting seedlings."},{"id":"c","text":"To selectively thin the stand for timber quality improvement."},{"id":"d","text":"To remove overstory trees and release the established regeneration."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00935', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Which Philippine species is most suited to regeneration through the coppice-with-standards silvicultural system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Swietenia macrophylla (Mahogany)"},{"id":"b","text":"Gmelina arborea (Yemane)"},{"id":"c","text":"Leucaena leucocephala (Ipil-ipil)"},{"id":"d","text":"Pinus kesiya (Benguet Pine)"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00936', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In an irregular shelterwood system, how is the regeneration of shade-intolerant species typically ensured?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By maintaining a continuous canopy to provide shade."},{"id":"b","text":"By immediately removing the entire canopy in one cut."},{"id":"c","text":"By planting shade-intolerant species under the existing canopy."},{"id":"d","text":"By gradually opening the canopy in stages to increase light levels."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00937', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'For a forest manager aiming to maintain continuous forest cover while promoting the regeneration of indigenous species, which silvicultural system is most suitable?',
