  ('fp-g00938', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In the context of silvicultural systems, what is a key characteristic of the group selection method when applied to dipterocarp forests?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It involves removing all trees in large areas for regeneration."},{"id":"b","text":"It maintains a uniform age structure across the forest."},{"id":"c","text":"It requires artificial regeneration with shade-tolerant species."},{"id":"d","text":"It involves selective cutting in small groups to facilitate natural regeneration."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00939', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In sustainable forest management, how does the application of an improvement cutting differ from a sanitation cutting?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Improvement cutting removes diseased trees; sanitation cutting enhances growth of desired species."},{"id":"b","text":"Both improvement and sanitation cuttings focus on aesthetic enhancements."},{"id":"c","text":"Improvement cutting enhances growth of desired species; sanitation cutting removes diseased or dead trees."},{"id":"d","text":"Improvement cutting is used for clearcutting; sanitation cutting is for planting preparation."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00940', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'What is a typical goal of using the strip clearcutting method over traditional clearcutting in terms of ecosystem impact?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To increase the speed of forest regeneration across the entire stand."},{"id":"b","text":"To maximize timber yield from each harvest."},{"id":"c","text":"To promote uniform age distribution among trees."},{"id":"d","text":"To minimize visual impact and reduce soil erosion."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00941', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'Which silvicultural method is best utilized for promoting regeneration in a forest stand that includes species with varying degrees of shade tolerance?',
