   '[{"id":"a","text":"Remove trees with the highest growth rate to allow others to catch up."},{"id":"b","text":"Cut trees at random to maintain natural patterns."},{"id":"c","text":"Remove the tallest trees to allow more sunlight to reach the understory."},{"id":"d","text":"Select trees that are diseased or deformed to improve overall stand health."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g01120', 'forest-production', 'forest-plantation', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'How does the basal area of a forest plantation influence management decisions?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It determines the amount of leaf litter available for soil fertility."},{"id":"b","text":"It influences the spacing decisions for future planting."},{"id":"c","text":"Basal area is used to calculate the total timber volume of the stand."},{"id":"d","text":"Basal area directly affects the growth rate of individual trees."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g01121', 'forest-production', 'forest-plantation', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'What is the significance of using a randomized complete block design (RCBD) in experimental plots within forest plantations?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"RCBD ensures maximum use of available planting space."},{"id":"b","text":"It minimizes the effects of soil variability on treatment comparisons."},{"id":"c","text":"RCBD allows for easier integration of new species into the plantation."},{"id":"d","text":"It standardizes growth conditions for all experimental trees."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g01122', 'forest-production', 'forest-plantation', 'Hard', 'mock',
   'In a forest plantation, why is it important to regularly monitor the leaf nutrient content of trees?',
